`--force` defeats the already-stamped guard: the six seeded values are all wrong, and every one of
them is replaced by the value derived from the transcript. Each stale number differs from its fresh
counterpart, so a `--force` that only rewrote some keys would leave a visible survivor.

Arithmetic, s-foxtrot: one turn, 12:00:00 → 12:09:00 = 540s = 9 minutes; tokens input 42, output 8,
cache creation 6, no cache read field = 0; model claude-fx-sonnet.

